WEBVTT

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.070
Takamura-san's world title match was finalized?

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.140
Yeah, it's in December.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.300
Wow,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.400
I joined the gym at a great time.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.200
I'm looking forward to it!

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.190
It's even better for us.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.080
We've been watching him since the beginning.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.500
He's finally gonna be number one in the world!

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.370
That's enough celebrating for now!

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.830
We still have the matches in October before then.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.070
That includes Takamura's preliminary match for his world title fight.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.460
We've also got Itagaki and Kimura in matches on that night, so both of you get ready!

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.100
Right!

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.100
Yes! {jama: added}

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.750
Can't let some low-level guy score an upset on me!

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.970
I'm in the opening match, so I'll take the lead!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.430
Things sure are heating up!

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.140
Whether we like it or not, he's the one who sets the pace for our gym.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.590
That includes you too, Ippo-kun.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.110
You're fighting in the match before Takamura-kun's world title fight in December.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.990
M-Me too!?

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.020
The opponent hasn't been decided yet,

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.740
but we're bound to sell out the arena with both our headliners, Takamura-kun and Ippo-kun fighting!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.870
Then the venue is in...

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.620
It's in Japan, of course!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.370
At Takamura-kun's request, it'll be the Ryogoku Kokugikan!

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.680
He said it felt manly there and,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.920
since it was the arena Date Eiji lost in, that he would make up for the disappointment!

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.760
<i>The Ryogoku Kokugikan...</i>

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.550
<i>I'll be fighting in the same ring that Date-san did!?</i>

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:19.800
<i>Okay!</i>

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.250
Yagi-san, I'll do my absolute best!

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.070
Right!

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:23.950
Hell yeah!

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.390
I'll do my best too!

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.370
You actually don't have a match scheduled.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.780
A-Aoki-san...

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.740
I can smell the stench of being left out.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.700
I heard about the world title challenge!

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.830
Huh?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.290
Where's Takamura-kun?

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.590
In the bathroom.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.710
He's been taking longer than usual lately.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.210
<i>All right... nothing in it.</i>

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.710
<i>I gotta make sure to check every time...</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.260
<i>in case something like that is in there again.</i>

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.660
<i>I can't believe I've gotta worry about this with my title match coming up.</i>

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.000
So, you've been constipated?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.270
I guess when it comes to something like this, even you get nervous.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.640
Me nervous!?

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.630
No way!

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.900
The champion's the one chickening out!

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.490
Cancelling the title match and then suddenly agreeing to it again...

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.030
Playing all these stupid mind games!

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.530
T-That was actually the manager's strategy in order to make sure they have the advantage.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.030
What?

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.110
It seems like Bryan Hawk is a hard fighter to manage.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.040
He has a wild personality and no one has ever actually witnessed him training.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.630
From what I understand, it's nearly impossible to get a hold of him unless it's the week before a match.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.820
He's famous for being the champion who hates to train.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.420
B-But he's the world champion!

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.220
How could he have done that without training?

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.500
He won using nothing but his natural born talent.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.100
Every now and then, a fighter like that will show up on the world stage.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.730
After he won the title,

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.230
he bragged about only having trained for nine days.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.990
O-Only nine days!?

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.580
He says he prefers to spend the time leading up to a match in bed with women.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.030
He's one cocky asshole!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.950
That has to be a bluff.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.090
There's no telling whether or not that's true,

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:12.330
but he's definitely strong.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.230
20 matches, 20 wins, 17 KO's.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.170
He took the belt without a scratch in America where competition in the jr. middleweights is particularly fierce.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:27.130
Well, he's up against the most dangerous man alive this time!

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:31.480
Little Hawk-kun is probably gonna be training his ass off while crying to himself!

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.790
The manager mentioned this while holding his head in his hands...

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.820
It seems they can't get a hold of him.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.400
W-Wait a second!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.240
He knows about the match, right!?

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.450
They were able to tell him that much.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.160
But...

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.490
But?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.010
When he heard the challenger was Japanese, he hung up.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.500
He's been missing ever since.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.210
He hung up without even asking who I was!?

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.260
Without even knowing my name...

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.510
<i>He hung up when he found out he was fighting someone Japanese!?</i>

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.090
<i>Americans dominate the heavier weight classes.</i>

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.770
<i>It's not surprising that he'd take someone from Japan lightly.</i>

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.760
<i>He doesn't train and he's not even interested in who he's fighting.</i>

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.510
<i>This guy is going too far, dammit!</i>

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.550
Don't get too worked up, Takamura.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:30.540
Just focus on the first match for now.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.750
I know, I know.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.040
Whether he trains or not doesn't matter.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.460
I'm gonna take the title and do it my way!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.620
And to top it off...

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.670
I'll kill him!

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.490
Hey, don't push!

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.990
It says this is the preliminary fight before a world title match!

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.160
I guess it really was finalized!

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.870
It's already that full!?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.050
That's exciting!

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.480
Be grateful to Takamura-san.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.830
Must be nice to be so carefree.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.220
Huh?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.220
Kimura-san, are you nervous?

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.090
Hey now, Mr. Veteran, get it together.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.260
It's my first match in a while and the first since I started spelling Tatsuya in katakana.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.810
It feels like a debut match.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.150
So you're the same as me!

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.100
You could be a little more nervous.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:43.610
Let's go, Itagaki!

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:46.740
Hey!

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.020
Do a good job, okay?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.240
Let's set the stage for Takamura-san's match.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.120
Well...

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.740
I intend to, but...

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.720
I have my own goal to chase after,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.830
so I'll get into the ring for myself this time.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.880
And now, a featherweight match scheduled for 4 rounds!

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:13.530
Since it's his debut match, there won't be much cheering.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.380
Let's shout out "Manabu!" to get him in the swing of things.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:17.850
Right!

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:24.630
In the red corner, weighing 125 and 1/2 pounds, from the Kamogawa Gym...

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:29.470
Itagaki Manabu!

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.470
Here we go...

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.220
Manabu-kun, good luck!

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.580
Please win!

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:38.000
What's with that huge crowd of college chicks!?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.370
S-Seems like a cheering squad.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:46.410
In the blue corner, weighing 125 and 3/4 pounds, from the Sayama Gym,

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.130
Makino Fumito!

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.640
Kinda plain looking, isn't he?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.720
The program says...

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.730
two matches and two losses.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.390
He hasn't won yet?

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:02.700
Itagaki's a super rookie who transferred over from the amateurs...

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.650
I'm surprised they accepted this match.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:09.150
Itagaki seems different than he did in the waiting room.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.700
What do you think, Champion?

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.090
I'm talking to you, dammit!

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:16.870
Oh, right!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.340
Well, it is his debut match.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.540
He looks tense...

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.770
but not stiff.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.250
I can sense his concentration.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.170
He looks good.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.170
He's used to fighting in front of big crowds.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:34.680
Compare that to his opponent who looks worried.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.080
He seems like he's going to do whatever it takes to win.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.200
He knows about your reputation, so he'll try and rush in to take the pace.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.520
Make sure you're careful!

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.860
<i>I feel like I'm locked in a cage...</i>

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.440
<i>So this is the pro ring?</i>

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.240
<i>I've got to dodge a punch first,</i>

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.680
<i>then I'll know what kind of condition I'm in today.</i>

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.740
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.890
<i>I've got to dodge a punch first,</i>

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:10.360
<i>then I'll know what kind of condition I'm in today.</i>

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:12.470
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.660
<i>I'm moving well!</i>

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.220
<i>My steps feel light!</i>

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:24.980
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.780
Oh, Manabu-kun!

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.780
He doesn't move like a rookie!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.490
You're so cool!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.490
Is this really his debut match!?

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:32.840
I hate to admit it, but Itagaki's boxing is smooth as hell.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.450
Right!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:38.960
So fast!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.450
How many times did he just hit him!?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.540
Amazing!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:42.860
Go for a KO!

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.170
Let's have a flashy debut fitting for the super rookie!

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:51.720
That's scary!

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:52.980
He's throwing huge swings!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.590
He's got no other choice!

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.220
The difference in speed is too great.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:02.100
He has to bet it all on a do-or-die punch or somehow draw him into a slugfest.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.060
<i>Nothing but full swings?</i>

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.830
<i>On the other hand, that makes it easy to aim for this!</i>

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.500
He paid him back double with a counter!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.190
He's keeping a cool head!

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.180
He nailed him!

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:13.820
You can do it, get him!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.190
<i>It's working!</i>

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:15.900
<i>I can do it!</i>

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:21.580
<i>I'll be taking the shortest route possible to Makunouchi-san's title.</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.910
<i>Like hell you will!</i>

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.000
<i>This time, I'll stop him!</i>

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.920
<i>I'll pay him back in the pro ring for our amateur days!</i>

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.920
<i>And I'm not taking any detours!</i>

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.020
Good idea, lay into him!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.550
<i>He looks desperate.</i>

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.000
<i>Is it because of Itagaki-kun?</i>

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:39.660
<i>No,</i>

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.050
<i>he looked like that before he even got into the ring.</i>

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.790
<i>What is it?</i>

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.940
<i>Look, Makino...</i>

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.940
<i>You have to show some potential. {Solo- TLC}</i>

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.800
<i>I know you love boxing,</i>

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.110
<i>but you're just gonna hurt yourself if you keep this up.</i>

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.830
<i>Lose this next match...</i>

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.330
<i>and you'll have to give it up.</i>

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.340
Look out, Itagaki-kun!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.510
Referee, he was butting just now!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:18.000
W-What the hell are you doing, dumbass!?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.340
You're wide open!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.670
Fight back!

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.530
What the hell is wrong with him!?

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:29.850
ONE

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.290
W-Why are you counting!?

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.430
TWO

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.310
What about the butting!?

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.920
This isn't a proper down!

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.290
THREE

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.820
I said it wasn't really a down!

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:37.430
FOUR

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.110
Itagaki-kun, calm down!

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.720
FIVE

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.400
Take your fighting pose!

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:41.750
SIX

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.030
Dammit... I'm fine.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.410
<i>His opponent was totally overwhelmed.</i>

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.660
<i>It's only natural that he'd do whatever he could to win.</i>

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.360
It's the pro ring...

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.480
there's no telling what can happen.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.500
He lost his cool and tried to make an appeal.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.160
That down is gonna cost him.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:01.580
There are a lot of cases where amateur boxers who fight nice and clean end up getting wiped out in rough fights.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.600
Oh, no...

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.100
Box!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.020
<i>Dammit... Dammit...</i>

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.180
Use your legs and regroup!

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.350
Stay calm!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.810
<i>There's a two knockdown limit in 4 round matches!</i>

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:16.770
<i>Don't fall down no matter what!</i>

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.570
<i>I'm not gonna get hit again!</i>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.140
<i>I can't afford...</i>

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:23.320
<i>any detours!</i>

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:27.290
An elbow!?

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.380
Stop! The match is over!

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.430
I-It can't be!

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:39.670
This can't...

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:43.650
That was an elbow, not a punch!

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.850
I'm not hurt at all! I can still go on!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.280
I can still...

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.130
Can't accept that you lost or something!?

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.870
Get outta the ring!

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.890
They need to start the next fight!

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.480
Throw him out already!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.090
You lost, got it!?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.690
You've already lost!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.910
I-Itagaki...

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.560
I-I can still fight...

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:06.410
I can still...

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:07.530
Itagaki!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.220
Better luck next time, dumbass!

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.630
You're pissing me off!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.790
Don't expect any sympathy!

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:21.490
Forget applause, now he's getting booed out of the arena!

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.420
This turned into the worst debut possible!

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.430
Itagaki-kun...

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.930
I-I'll go to his dressing room!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.150
Please cheer Kimura-san on for me!

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.040
Yeah, don't worry about it.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.940
He's an even better underdog hunter than I am!

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:38.470
Next, the bout before the main event!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:41.190
A 10 round jr. lightweight match!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:42.890
It's Kimura!

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.250
It's been a long time!

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.770
We're counting on you!

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:47.700
You'll be the one to win the belt next!

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:50.240
Fight Mashiba again!

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.430
It's started...

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.330
Don't worry, Kimura-san's a veteran.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.010
He won't lose to someone on a lower level than him.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.780
Itagaki-kun...

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:11.720
Um...

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.510
My opponent was on a lower level than me too.

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:18.770
I didn't intend to screw up either, but...

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.510
It was your debut match, so you were just tense.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.530
Is that how it looked?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:27.410
No.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.740
Actually, you looked good.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.930
I could follow his punches.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:34.540
There's no way a telegraphed punch like that could ever land on me. {Solo-  The term telegraphed is a valid boxing term}

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.820
His head and elbow did though.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:37.870
He cheated!

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.170
Itagaki-kun...

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:48.960
Where the hell was the referee looking!?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.450
How could he let two fouls slide like that!?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.430
Itagaki-kun, you'll hurt your hand!

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.190
You understand! Right, Senpai!?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.430
He was cheating!

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:00.150
It doesn't feel like I was even boxing!

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.660
What the hell!?

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:03.440
Why?

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.940
Why did I have to lose?

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.410
Did you see your opponent's face?

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.940
He looked really desperate.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.960
He must have had some reason why he couldn't afford to lose.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.850
That's why...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.160
So it's okay to foul someone if you win?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.240
Wow...

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.720
I guess anything can happen in the pros.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:31.430
It wasn't a foul.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.930
The referee didn't stop him.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:38.980
Maybe he thought they were unintentional or maybe he just didn't see them.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.760
Either way, you got distracted during the match.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.720
It's your own fault.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.480
If you had been as desperate as he was,

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.740
you would have fought back even after the headbutt.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.750
Sen... pai...

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:01.920
The possibility that anything can happen is a condition of fighting in the pro ring.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.250
That's enough!

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:06.580
I thought you were on my side.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.040
Screw the pro ring!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:08.970
I can't believe this.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.470
Itagaki-kun!

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:22.850
<i>I should have told him sooner.</i>

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.820
<i>I started noticing when we sparred at the beach.</i>

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.320
<i>His speed and technique are both perfect,</i>

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>but he didn't throw a single punch that felt dangerous!</i>

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.180
<i>Ambition and intensity...</i>

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:40.050
<i>Most pros can recognize those things just by looking at someone,</i>

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:42.960
<i>and Itagaki-kun didn't have enough of either.</i>

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:51.040
Hey, so how's Itagaki?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.260
He ran out.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.050
I think I was too hard on him.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:56.830
He was depressed too.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.650
I feel really bad.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.480
Don't worry about it.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.190
Give him a few days and he'll show up at the gym again.

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.440
I hope so.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:07.380
How's Kimura-san doing?

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.360
The tenth round is next.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.360
The final round!?

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.160
It sure is taking a long time.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.370
He's really beat up!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.740
Is his opponent strong!?

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:22.360
He's a genuine underdog.

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:24.130
W-What are the points at!?

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.080
By my count, I'd say they're even.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.040
How can that be!?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.760
Round 10. Final round! {jama: added}

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.050
<i>All right! {jama: added}</i>

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.180
<i>I'm really gonna let him have it!</i>

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.680
<i>Dragon Fish Blow!</i>

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.370
That kind of big swing...

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.480
It doesn't suit Kimura-san at all.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.440
His only saving grace has been that his opponent's punches are crappy.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:56.850
It's his first match in a long time, so I think he's forgotten his original style and is just trying to KO him.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.740
He's been going full steam the whole time and now it's the tenth round...

00:16:58.740 --> 00:16:59.830
<i>Damn you.</i>

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.410
<i>Fall, fall already!</i>

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.420
You're putting too much of your shoulder into it!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.410
Throw smaller, more compact punches!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:10.630
Stop!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.630
The match is over!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:16.450
It... It went to a decision...

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.930
Did he lose the final round?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.560
<i>Crap...</i>

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.250
<i>I wanted to KO him, but it went to a decision.</i>

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.950
<i>I had the point lead, right?</i>

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.570
<i>I won, right?</i>

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.830
<i>What the hell's taking so long?</i>

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.070
<i>Figure it out already!</i>

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.570
<i>It can't be that I—</i>

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.620
Red corner, Kimura!

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.350
Hell yeah!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:44.730
Seriously? That scoring seems kind of fishy.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.730
Wasn't it Kimura who lost!?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.930
He got saved by a hometown decision!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.090
I'll do better next time.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.020
I wonder what's up with today?

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:56.090
Even Kimura-san...

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:59.770
They're not showing any results from the training camp at the beach.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:02.550
Some underdog hunter he ended up being!

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:04.500
I never said I was any kind of hunter!

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.220
Kimura-san!

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.950
Dammit...

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:09.600
I wanted to set the stage for Takamura-san's match too.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:12.290
The Kamogawa Gym has three shots...

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:15.110
We'll have to bet it all on the last one!

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:16.610
Right!

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:23.200
We will now begin tonight's main event, a 10 round jr. middleweight match!

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:25.220
It's Takamura!

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.130
He's got his bearskin on!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.660
I've been waiting for you Takamura!

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:32.210
The reaction from the crowd when the star arrives is definitely different.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:35.610
He should be able to blow the dark clouds away!

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:43.090
Tonight, an archangel descends upon Korakuen Hall along with his great ambitions!

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:54.850
He's stumbling around!

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.580
What kinda performance is that?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.610
He's always a hoot to watch!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.140
He's taking the fur off!

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:02.200
Hurry and show your face!

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.370
Takamura!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.950
Takamura!

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:06.180
Taka... {jama: added}

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:07.500
Just listen to these huge crowds,

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:12.330
ringing with antici... pa... tion?

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.230
What the hell? He shrunk!?

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:17.510
What's going on?

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:19.660
He...

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:22.780
He totally screwed up his weight management.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:27.520
The dark clouds just got darker.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:29.980
This is too dangerous.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:33.520
Did he shut himself up in the bathroom before the match?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:37.020
Something about being constipated?

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.240
It's not my fault!

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:45.280
Facing him is the Filipino Middleweight Champion, Morris West!

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:49.450
He intends to make an impact in the world rankings with a victory today!

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:52.010
H-He looks strong.

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.380
And he's in perfect condition.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:58.130
<i>Dammit, it's gonna be my fault if he loses.</i>

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.260
<i>Please win, Takamura-san!</i>

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.260
Overwork from getting carried away with your training...

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.230
Constipation from dehydrating yourself because of the weight management...

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:08.360
I can't imagine you'll be able to move around properly.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:10.560
But this is the prelude to your world title match!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.020
You can't afford to screw this up!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.150
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.210
I'm gonna handle this like...

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:21.550
He tipped over.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.780
Is he gonna be able to punch properly?

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.090
Dark clouds gather over Korakuen Hall!

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:28.230
But there will be no delays!

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:30.540
The bell for this climactic battle has now...

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:35.640
been sounded!
